##Find Second highest salary of an employee?##

2 approach here--> NOT IN   operator and < operator     
 /Here we first creating a result set excluding first highest salary i.e max(sal)
Again applying max(sal) on the result would fetch the second highest salary.



SELECT max(sal) FROM emp
WHERE sal NOT IN (SELECT max(sal) FROM emp);



SELECT max(sal) FROM emp
WHERE sal < (SELECT max(sal) FROM emp);
